Package: pyrt
Title: Runtime Support for Converted 'Python' Packages
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yee How", "Lau", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "lauyeehow1986@gmail.com")
  )
Description: Provides the 'Python' runtime semantics required by 'R' packages
    generated with 'pyport', including reference-semantics containers, class
    and method-resolution-order dispatch, exception hierarchies, iteration and
    slicing helpers, arbitrary-precision integer arithmetic, and bit-exact
    random number generation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/lauyeehow1986-hub/r_python_converter
BugReports: https://github.com/lauyeehow1986-hub/r_python_converter/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports:
    gmp (>= 0.7-1),
    R6 (>= 2.5.1),
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
